 ## Background[m
 [m
[31m-The indicators come from a sequential multi-method study with eight family medicine groups in Quebec (2021-2022):[m
[31m-a systematic review of 81 papers on advanced access, a 17-member expert committee, and extraction from three EMR[m
[31m-products. Six indicators could be extracted reliably and went into a dynamic dashboard, together with a demand and[m
[31m-supply profile for each physician:[m
[32m+[m[32mOn the CHUS / Université de Sherbrooke access-to-care project (eight GMFs in Quebec, three EMR products), we built a dashboard from the six indicators that could be extracted reliably from every EMR, plus a demand and supply profile per physician:[m
 [m
 > Breton M, Gaboury I, Bordeleau F, Lamoureux-Lamarche C, Martin É, Deslauriers V, Deville-Stoetzel J-B.[m
 > *Use of Electronic Medical Record Data to Create a Dashboard on Access to Primary Care.*[m
 > Healthcare Policy. 2023;18(4):72-88. doi:10.12927/hcpol.2023.27092[m
 [m
[31m-This project is the visualization layer. The indicators themselves are computed by the companion C++ engine[m
