 ## Limitations[m
 [m
[31m-* Distances are straight lines, not road travel times, and supply is a head count of physicians, not full-time[m
[31m-  equivalents.[m
[31m-* Registration is a snapshot; changes of family physician during the period are not modelled.[m
[31m-* Area-level measures only cover visits to the clinics in the extract. Residents who use other clinics are invisible.[m
[31m-* The synthetic gradients illustrate the views and say nothing about any real population.[m
[32m+[m[32mDistances are straight lines, not travel times on roads, and supply is a head count of physicians, not full-time equivalents. Registration is a snapshot, so changes of family physician during the period are ignored. Area measures only cover visits to the clinics in the extract: residents who go elsewhere are simply invisible. And of course, the synthetic gradients are only there to show what the views can do; they say nothing about a real population.[m
